WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
Picture a worker earning 15 an hour,

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.780
who chooses to work 36 hours a week.

3
00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.530
Now the pay rises to 25 an hour.

4
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.920
And the worker chooses
to work only 34 hours.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.550
Higher pay, yet fewer hours.

6
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.070
So what makes people willing to do a job,

7
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.670
and why isn't the pay the whole story?

8
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.320
In this mission, you'll see
why the supply of labour

9
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.180
to a job slopes upward,

10
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.690
and what shifts it.

11
00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:29.980
Then you'll test how wages and
jobs respond when demand rises,

12
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.280
in a graph lab.

13
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.480
Your mission: find out what
really decides how much

14
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.440
labour people are willing to supply.
